From: shadaytree <82917003+shadaytree@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:23:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] test(sim): plunge_depth_tab pins the pecked tab window dives

PR #3866 (#3678) made each tab window dive of the 2d/contour-tabs case
peck one stepdown at a time, and merged before PR #3847 (#3679), whose
test pinned the three dives that the verifier named. Main went red.

The test now pins that the verifier names no PlungeTooDeep finding, and
that tab windows 1 to 3 each peck Z4, Z2, Z0 with no feed more than the
2 mm stepdown below the depth before it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Fixes #3920
